\pard\nowidctlpar\sb120\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs18\lang1033 About HID Hide\par

\pard\nowidctlpar\sa200\sl276\slmult1 Purpose of \cf2 HID Hide\cf0  is to hide original (physical) controllers from games, so that only virtual controllers are visible. Install \cf2 HID Hide\cf0  only if the original controller prevents the virtual controller from functioning properly in a game.\par
Install: \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Options\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  tab \f1\u8594?\f0\lang1033  \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Virtual Device\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  tab \f1\u8594?\f0\lang1033  HID Hide \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Install\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  button.\line Uninstall: \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Options\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  tab \f1\u8594?\f0\lang1033  \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Virtual Device\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  tab \f1\u8594?\f0\lang1033  HID Hide \cf3\lang1063 [\lang1033 Uninstall\lang1063 ]\cf0\lang1033  button.\par
\cf2 HID Hide\cf0  is configured externally using the \cf2 HID Hide Configuration Client\cf0  application, which is installed alongside the driver. Use that application to select which devices to hide and which applications are allowed to see hidden devices.\par
\cf2 HID Hide\cf0  is the modern replacement for the older \cf2 HID Guardian\cf0  driver. Unlike HID Guardian, HID Hide does \cf2 not\cf0  risk blocking access to your keyboard or mouse.\par
For more information, visit:\par

